# Cloudflare Pages merges headers of ALL matching rules (no override), so
# two rules that both set Cache-Control for the same path emit two header
# lines. We keep the rules disjoint in effect: /contact/* carries no-store
# (strongest directive wins the merge, so the form page is never edge-cached),
# and everything else carries one clean HTML caching policy.
#
# Speed fix (2026-09-14, P0): HTML cold requests were hitting a 5.6-8.5s origin
# because the edge TTL was only 300s + must-revalidate. Now:
#   - CF edge:   s-maxage=3600 (1h) + stale-while-revalidate=86400 (24h)
#                -> after the 1h, stale HTML is served instantly while CF
#                revalidates in the background; users/bots never hit cold origin.
#   - Browser:   max-age=300 (unchanged 5-min revalidate, no worse for visitors).
# CF honours s-maxage over max-age for edge caching. The zone cache rule
# "wanlian911 HTML edge cache" stays in "respect origin / age-from-header" mode,
# so it now picks up the 3600s from here.

/contact/*
  Cache-Control: no-store, no-cache, must-revalidate
  Pragma: no-cache
  Expires: 0

/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, s-maxage=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400
